========================================================================
STEP 0 — INSPECT v0 EVIDENCE
========================================================================

1. Find the latest v0 run JSON:
   Get-ChildItem runs/*v0*.json | Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1

2. Read the run JSON. Focus on:
   - results[*].result.observed_mismatch — what the grader flagged
   - results[*].result.failures — why each case failed
   - results[*].result.actual_tool_calls — what the agent actually did
   - summary.case_accuracy, summary.tool_routing_accuracy,
     summary.argument_accuracy, summary.multiturn_accuracy
   - summary.provider_error_cases (must be 0)
   - summary.measured_cases (must equal total_cases)

3. Identify the ROOT CAUSE pattern:
   The current system_prompt.md tells the agent:
     - "do not ask questions, just guess"
     - "just go ahead and send without confirmation"
     - "always finish in a single step"
   This DIRECTLY contradicts eval cases:
     - R10 (missing_handle → expect clarify)
     - R11 (missing_url → expect clarify)
     - R12 (confirm_before_send → expect clarify yes_no)
     - R08, R14 (out_of_scope → expect refuse, no tool)
     - R09 (no_tool_meta → expect answer_without_tool)
     - M01-M06 (multi-turn → needs multi-step support)

========================================================================
STEP 1 — FIX system_prompt.md (ONLY this file)
========================================================================

Rewrite artifacts/system_prompt.md to:

a) Replace "don't ask questions" with a clarification policy:
   - If user query is missing critical info (handle, URL), call clarify
   - Map names to handles: Sam Altman → sama, Elon Musk → elonmusk, Andrej Karpathy → karpathy
   - Before destructive actions (send/post), call clarify(response_type="yes_no")

b) Add out-of-scope behavior:
   - Coding, math, general knowledge NOT about research/news → refuse politely, no tool call
   - Meta questions about the agent → answer directly with no tool call

c) Add multi-turn support:
   - Carry context from previous turns (screenname, limit, timeframe, topic, query)
   - Latest user instruction overrides earlier ones
   - If user explicitly switches topic/tool, follow the latest intent

d) Keep it concise — one page max, bullet-friendly.

IMPORTANT: Only edit artifacts/system_prompt.md in this round.

